fact WorkItem(id: "WI-620", description: some(value: "Grammar: parenthesized lambda patterns don't parse as contract-clause call arguments: 'ensures all_match(xs, lambda x -> gt(x, 0))' parses, but 'ensures all_match(xs, lambda (x) -> gt(x, 0))' is a syntax error (same for tuple/annotated params, which REQUIRE parens — so multi-param and annotated lambdas are unwritable in requires/ensures argument position; rule bodies accept both spellings). Found empirically during WI-618 /code-review. Fix in tree-sitter grammar: admit the parenthesized lambda-param form wherever contract-clause arguments admit lambda_expr. ACCEPTANCE: both spellings parse in requires/ensures; grammar corpus + cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-03T07:19:35Z"))
